<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<title>Firsts, drawn in code</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Comic+Neue:wght@400;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
:root{
  --page:#dfe9ef; --ink:#15212b; --muted:#566775; --panel:#ffffff; --line:#c3d1db; --accent:#2f5a9e;
  box-sizing:border-box; padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px); padding-bottom:env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px);
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]){ --page:#10161b; --ink:#e7eef3; --muted:#91a2af; --panel:#1a2229; --line:#2b3843; --accent:#7ea6e6; }
}
:root[data-theme="dark"]{ --page:#10161b; --ink:#e7eef3; --muted:#91a2af; --panel:#1a2229; --line:#2b3843; --accent:#7ea6e6; }
html{ scroll-padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px); }
*,*::before,*::after{ box-sizing:inherit; }
body{ margin:0; background:var(--page); color:var(--ink); font-family:'Comic Neue','Comic Sans MS','Chalkboard SE',cursive,sans-serif; }
main{ max-width:1320px; margin:0 auto; padding:24px 20px 40px; }
h1{ font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3.2vw,2.3rem); margin:0 0 4px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:-0.01em; }
.sub{ margin:0 0 18px; color:var(--muted); font-size:1.05rem; max-width:62ch; }
.stage{ position:relative; width:100%; aspect-ratio:16/9; background:#c3e7f8; border-radius:6px; overflow:hidden; border:2px solid var(--ink); }
canvas{ width:100%; height:100%; display:block; }
.caption{ min-height:3.2em; margin:14px 0 10px; font-size:clamp(1.05rem,2vw,1.35rem); line-height:1.4; max-width:70ch; }
.caption[hidden]{ display:block; visibility:hidden; }
.bar{ display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:center; gap:10px; }
button{ font:inherit; font-weight:700; font-size:1rem; color:var(--ink); background:var(--panel); border:2px solid var(--ink); border-radius:999px; padding:8px 16px; cursor:pointer; min-height:44px; }
button:hover{ background:var(--line); }
button:focus-visible, input:focus-visible{ outline:3px solid var(--accent); outline-offset:2px; }
button.play{ background:var(--ink); color:var(--page); min-width:96px; }
.count{ margin-left:auto; color:var(--muted); font-size:1rem; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }
.opts{ display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:18px; margin-top:14px; color:var(--muted); }
label{ display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; cursor:pointer; }
input[type=checkbox]{ width:20px; height:20px; accent-color:var(--accent); }
.scrub{ display:flex; gap:4px; margin:12px 0 0; }
.scrub span{ flex:1; height:8px; border-radius:4px; background:var(--line); cursor:pointer; }
.scrub span.on{ background:var(--ink); }
.scrub span.done{ background:var(--muted); }
@media (max-width:600px){ .count{ margin-left:0; width:100%; } }
.editor{ margin-top:22px; border:2px solid var(--ink); border-radius:10px; background:var(--panel); }
.editor summary{ cursor:pointer; font-weight:700; font-size:1.15rem; padding:12px 16px; min-height:44px; }
.ed-grid{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,420px),1fr)); gap:16px; padding:0 16px 16px; }
.editor fieldset{ border:2px solid var(--line); border-radius:8px; padding:12px 14px; margin:0; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:12px; min-width:0; }
.editor legend{ font-weight:700; padding:0 6px; }
.editor label{ flex-wrap:wrap; }
.editor select, .editor input[type=number]{ font:inherit; font-size:1rem; color:var(--ink); background:var(--page); border:2px solid var(--line); border-radius:6px; padding:6px 8px; min-height:40px; }
.editor input[type=number]{ width:6.5em; }
.editor input[type=range]{ flex:1; min-width:140px; accent-color:var(--accent); }
.editor .row{ display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:10px; align-items:center; }
.editor .hint{ margin:0; color:var(--muted); font-size:0.95rem; }
.editor progress{ flex:1; min-width:160px; height:14px; accent-color:var(--accent); }
.editor button:disabled{ opacity:0.5; cursor:default; }
.filebtn{ font-weight:700; border:2px solid var(--ink); border-radius:999px; padding:8px 16px; min-height:44px; background:var(--panel); }
.filebtn input{ position:absolute; width:1px; height:1px; opacity:0; }
.filebtn:focus-within{ outline:3px solid var(--accent); outline-offset:2px; }
.editor h3{ margin:4px 0 0; font-size:1.05rem; }
.help{ padding:0 16px 16px; }
.help details{ border:2px solid var(--line); border-radius:8px; padding:0 14px; margin-top:10px; }
.help summary{ font-size:1.05rem; padding:12px 0; min-height:0; }
.help ol, .help ul{ margin:0 0 12px; padding-left:1.4em; line-height:1.5; }
.help p{ margin:0 0 10px; line-height:1.5; max-width:80ch; }
.help kbd{ font:inherit; font-weight:700; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:4px; padding:0 4px; }
.scrub span.wob{ box-shadow:0 4px 0 -1px #e0892a; }
.wf{ margin:0 16px 16px; border:2px solid var(--ink); border-radius:8px; padding:0 14px 14px; display:block; }
.wf > summary{ padding:12px 0; }
.wf .row{ margin:10px 0; }
.wf-grid{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(min(100%,210px),1fr)); gap:10px; }
.wf-grid figure{ margin:0; border:3px solid var(--line); border-radius:8px; padding:6px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:6px; }
.wf-grid figure.on{ border-color:#e0892a; }
.wf-grid .wf-show{ padding:0; border:0; border-radius:4px; background:none; min-height:0; cursor:zoom-in; display:block; width:100%; }
.wf-grid canvas{ width:100%; height:auto; aspect-ratio:16/9; display:block; border-radius:4px; }
.tl{ padding:0 16px 16px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px; }
.tl h3{ margin:0; }
.tl-wrap{ max-height:460px; overflow:auto; border:2px solid var(--line); border-radius:8px; }
.tl table{ border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font-size:0.95rem; }
.tl th, .tl td{ padding:3px 8px; text-align:left; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); white-space:nowrap; }
.tl thead th{ position:sticky; top:0; z-index:1; background:var(--panel); }
.tl td.tl-nar{ white-space:nowrap; overflow:hidden; text-overflow:ellipsis; max-width:28em; color:var(--muted); }
.tl tbody tr.cur{ background:var(--line); }
.tl tbody tr.wob td:first-child{ box-shadow:inset 4px 0 0 #e0892a; }
.editor .tl td select, .editor .tl td input[type=number]{ min-height:34px; padding:2px 6px; font-size:0.95rem; }
.editor .tl td input[type=number]{ width:5em; }
.tl-go{ min-height:34px; padding:2px 10px; font-size:0.95rem; border-width:1px; }
.vh{ position:absolute; width:1px; height:1px; overflow:hidden; clip:rect(0 0 0 0); white-space:nowrap; }
@media (max-width:700px){ .tl .tl-nar{ display:none; } }
[hidden]{ display:none !important; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <h1>Firsts, drawn in code</h1>
  <p class="sub">The whole video: the opening grid, all nine firsts, and the closing grid. Open <b>Edit &amp; export</b> below to set each panel's length, wobble and zoom, then save it as video or pictures for Premiere Pro, After Effects or any editor.</p>
  <div class="stage"><canvas id="cv" width="1920" height="1080" aria-label="Current panel"></canvas></div>
  <p class="caption" id="cap" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <div class="bar">
    <button id="prev" aria-label="Previous panel">Back</button>
    <button id="play" class="play">Play</button>
    <button id="next" aria-label="Next panel">Next</button>
    <button id="restart">Start over</button>
    <button id="wfOpen" type="button" title="See this panel's wobble frames, pick the ones you like and save them">Wobble frames</button>
    <span class="count" id="count"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="scrub" id="scrub" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="opts">
    <label><input type="checkbox" id="optCap" checked> Show narration</label>
    <label><input type="checkbox" id="optText" checked> Show written text (dates, labels)</label>
    <label><input type="checkbox" id="optName" checked> Name in the title bar</label>
  </div>
  <details class="editor" id="editor">
    <summary>Edit &amp; export</summary>
    <div class="ed-grid">
      <fieldset>
        <legend>This panel: <span id="edPanel"></span></legend>
        <label>Length <input type="number" id="edDur" min="0.3" max="60" step="0.1" inputmode="decimal"> seconds</label>
        <label>Wobble <select id="edWob"></select></label>
        <label>Zoom <select id="edZoom"></select></label>
        <label>Zoom amount <input type="range" id="edAmt" min="2" max="40" step="1"> <output id="edAmtOut"></output></label>
        <p class="hint">To choose where the zoom goes, pause and click that spot on the picture. Press Play to watch it, wobble included.</p>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="edGuide"> Show where the zoom ends (red dashed frame, only here, never in exports)</label>
        <label>Written text <select id="edText"><option value="default">Follow the switch above</option><option value="on">On</option><option value="off">Off</option></select></label>
        <div class="row"><button id="edItem" type="button">Use for this whole item</button><button id="edAll" type="button">Use for every panel</button><button id="edReset" type="button">Reset this panel</button></div>
      </fieldset>
      <fieldset>
        <legend>Export</legend>
        <label>What <select id="exWhat"><option value="all">Whole video</option><option value="item">This item</option><option value="panel">This panel</option><option value="ticked">Panels ticked in the list below</option><option value="range">Panels from … to …</option></select></label>
        <label id="exRange" hidden>From panel <input type="number" id="exFrom" value="3" min="1" max="221"> to <input type="number" id="exTo" value="23" min="1" max="221"></label>
        <label>Size <select id="exRes"><option value="1">1080p (1920×1080)</option><option value="1.3333">1440p (2560×1440)</option><option value="2">4K (3840×2160)</option></select></label>
        <label>Frame rate <select id="exFps"><option value="24">24 fps</option><option value="25">25 fps</option><option value="30">30 fps</option><option value="60">60 fps</option></select></label>
        <label>Video quality <select id="exQ"><option value="1">Good (smaller file)</option><option value="2">High</option><option value="3">Best (biggest file)</option></select></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="exBar"> Title bar in videos</label>
        <label>Pictures and wobble loops <select id="exLayersMode"><option value="flat">Everything in one picture</option><option value="twopart">Title bar separate</option><option value="split">Drawing, text and title bar all separate</option></select></label>
        <label>Wobble speed <select id="exBoil"><option value="6">Slow</option><option value="8">Normal</option><option value="12">Fast</option></select></label>
        <label>Wobble frames per loop <select id="exFrames"><option value="3">3</option><option value="4">4</option><option value="6">6</option><option value="8">8</option></select></label>
        <label>Wobble strength <input type="range" id="exAmp" min="0.5" max="3" step="0.1"></label>
        <label>Wobble loops as <select id="exWobFmt"><option value="mp4">MP4, already wobbling for the panel's length</option><option value="png">PNG frames, to loop yourself</option></select></label>
        <h3>Video</h3>
        <div class="row">
          <button id="exMp4" class="play ex-btn" type="button">One MP4</button>
          <button id="exClips" class="ex-btn" type="button">One MP4 per panel</button>
          <button id="exWobble" class="ex-btn" type="button">Wobble loops</button>
        </div>
        <h3>Pictures</h3>
        <div class="row">
          <button id="exPics" class="ex-btn" type="button">Pictures (PNG)</button>
          <button id="exFrames2" class="ex-btn" type="button">Every frame as PNG (best quality)</button>
        </div>
        <label>Start from frame <input type="number" id="exStart" min="1" value="1" step="1" inputmode="numeric"></label>
        <p class="hint">For "Every frame as PNG". If an export stopped, you don't need this: pick the same folder again and it carries on by itself from the last good frame. Type a number here only for ZIP downloads, or to redo from a certain frame.</p>
        <p class="hint">Wobble shows in the videos only on panels whose Wobble is on. Set it here for one panel, or tick panels in the list below and set them all at once.</p>
        <div class="row"><button id="exSave" type="button">Save settings</button><label class="filebtn">Load settings<input type="file" id="exLoad" accept=".json,application/json"></label></div>
        <div class="row"><progress id="exProg" max="1" value="0" hidden></progress><button id="exCancel" type="button" hidden>Cancel</button></div>
        <p id="exMsg" class="hint" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </fieldset>
    </div>
    <details class="wf" id="wf">
      <summary>Pick the wobble frames for panel <span id="wfPanel"></span></summary>
      <p class="hint">Every picture here is the panel on screen with a different wobble. Tick the ones you like and this panel loops only those, in the preview, the videos and the wobble exports. Click a picture to see it big above. The "Wobble" setting above chooses what wobbles. Go to another panel to pick for that one.</p>
      <div class="row"><button id="wfPlay" type="button">Play the loop</button><button id="wfMore" type="button">Show 8 more</button><button id="wfAuto" type="button">Clear my picks</button></div>
      <p id="wfMsg" class="hint" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      <div id="wfGrid" class="wf-grid"></div>
      <div class="row"><button id="wfPng" class="ex-btn" type="button">Save these frames (PNG)</button><button id="wfMp4" class="ex-btn" type="button">Save as a looping MP4</button></div>
    </details>
    <section class="tl" aria-labelledby="tlHead">
      <h3 id="tlHead">All panels</h3>
      <p class="hint">Set each panel's wobble, zoom and length right in the list, or tick several and set them together. Shift-click a tick box to tick every panel in between. Click a number to show that panel.</p>
      <div class="row">Tick: <button id="tlAll" type="button">All</button><button id="tlNone" type="button">None</button><button id="tlItem" type="button">This item</button><button id="tlWobbling" type="button">Ones that wobble</button></div>
      <div class="row">For the <b id="tlCount">0 panels</b> ticked:
        <label>Wobble <select id="tlWob"></select></label><button id="tlWobGo" type="button">Set</button>
        <label>Zoom <select id="tlZoom"></select></label><button id="tlZoomGo" type="button">Set</button>
        <label>Length <input type="number" id="tlLen" min="0.3" max="60" step="0.1" value="3" inputmode="decimal"> s</label><button id="tlLenGo" type="button">Set</button>
      </div>
      <div class="tl-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col"><span class="vh">Tick</span></th><th scope="col">#</th><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col" class="tl-nar">Narration</th><th scope="col">Length (s)</th><th scope="col">Wobble</th><th scope="col">Zoom</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody id="tlBody"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="help">
      <details>
        <summary>Which export do I want?</summary>
        <ul>
          <li><b>One MP4:</b> the finished video, with your lengths, wobble and zooms baked in. Nothing left to do in the editor.</li>
          <li><b>One MP4 per panel:</b> the same, cut into one clip per panel, so you can swap, trim or retime panels. Each comes with <i>timing.csv</i>.</li>
          <li><b>Wobble loops:</b> each panel wobbling on its own, with no zoom, so you can zoom it yourself. As MP4 it already wobbles for the panel's whole length; as PNG you get a few frames to loop. With one panel chosen you get that panel; with more, you get the panels whose Wobble is on.</li>
          <li><b>Pictures (PNG):</b> one still per panel, with no wobble or zoom. You do the movement yourself in the editor.</li>
          <li><b>Every frame as PNG:</b> the video as numbered, lossless pictures. The sharpest option, but a lot of files (the whole video is about 26,000 pictures and many gigabytes). In Chrome or Edge they go straight into a folder you pick; in other browsers they come as ZIP files of up to 1.5 GB each. If it stops, pick the same folder again and it carries on from where it stopped.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>For the sharpest result pick <b>4K</b>, even for a 1080p video: your editor shrinks it, and zooms stay crisp. <b>High</b> quality is plenty for YouTube; <b>Best</b> makes bigger files.</p>
        <p>A long export takes a while. The bar shows how long is left. It keeps going if you switch to another tab, but keep this tab open and the computer awake.</p>
        <p><b>Save into a folder that isn't synced to OneDrive, iCloud or Dropbox</b> (for example make <i>C:\Firsts export</i>). On Windows, Desktop and Documents are often in OneDrive: it tries to upload every picture while they're being saved, which can make saving fail, and it fills up your OneDrive.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Wobble on only some parts</summary>
        <p>Wobble is set per panel, and the videos only wobble where you turned it on. Four choices:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Off:</b> still.</li>
          <li><b>Lines wobble, people still:</b> the background and objects wobble, the people stay steady.</li>
          <li><b>People wobble, the rest still:</b> only the people wobble.</li>
          <li><b>Everything wobbles.</b></li>
        </ul>
        <p>To do many at once, tick them in <b>All panels</b> (shift-click ticks a run), pick the wobble and press <b>Set</b>. Then export <b>One MP4</b>: those panels wobble and the rest stay still. Or export only the wobbling ones with <b>Wobble loops</b>.</p>
        <p><b>To get the exact wobble of one picture:</b> go to that panel and press <b>Wobble frames</b> under the player. You see that panel drawn with different wobbles (frames 1, 2, 3… are the ones the preview plays). Click one to see it big, tick the ones you want, press <b>Play the loop</b> to check, then <b>Save these frames (PNG)</b> or <b>Save as a looping MP4</b>. You get only that panel, only those frames.</p>
        <p><b>For several chosen panels:</b> set their Wobble in <b>All panels</b>, pick <b>What: Panels ticked in the list below</b>, and press <b>Wobble loops</b>.</p>
        <p>With <b>Wobble loops as PNG frames</b>: in After Effects import the first frame as a PNG Sequence, right-click it &gt; <b>Interpret Footage &gt; Main</b>, set the frame rate to 8 (6 if Wobble speed is Slow, 12 if Fast) and <b>Loop</b> to 99. Premiere Pro can't loop a clip, so there the MP4 version is easier.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Together or separate: what's the difference?</summary>
        <p><b>Everything in one picture:</b> drag it in and you're done. The title bar, text and drawing move together.</p>
        <p><b>Separate:</b> the drawing, the text and the title bar come as different files. Each is full size with a see-through background, so stacked on tracks they line up by themselves. Put the title bar on the top track (V3), the text under it (V2) and the drawing at the bottom (V1). Use it when you want to zoom the drawing while the title bar stays still, or fade the text in and out yourself.</p>
        <p>If you zoom the drawing, zoom its text with it: select both, then <b>Nest</b> (Premiere Pro, right-click) or <b>Pre-compose</b> (After Effects, Layer menu), and zoom the nest.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Zoom-ins</summary>
        <p><b>Here:</b> choose <b>Push in</b> (or Pull out), set the amount, pause and click where it should zoom to, then press Play to check. The One MP4 exports include it.</p>
        <p><b>Yourself, in Premiere Pro or After Effects:</b> every export comes with <i>timing.csv</i> (opens in Excel). For each panel it gives the numbers to type:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Select the drawing. Premiere Pro: <b>Effect Controls &gt; Motion</b>. After Effects: open <b>Transform</b>.</li>
          <li>Set <b>Anchor Point</b> and <b>Position</b> to <i>anchor_x, anchor_y</i>. (If the files are bigger than your sequence, use <i>position_x_in_1080p, position_y_in_1080p</i> for Position.)</li>
          <li>On the panel's first frame, click the stopwatch beside <b>Scale</b> and type <i>scale_start</i>.</li>
          <li>On its last frame, type <i>scale_end</i>.</li>
          <li>Smooth it: Premiere Pro, right-click the keyframes &gt; <b>Temporal Interpolation &gt; Ease In / Ease Out</b>. After Effects, select both and press <kbd>F9</kbd>.</li>
        </ol>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Putting it into Premiere Pro or After Effects</summary>
        <ol>
          <li><b>Import:</b> File &gt; Import. For a numbered set of pictures (a wobble folder or <i>frames</i>), click only the first file and tick <b>Image Sequence</b> (Premiere) or <b>PNG Sequence</b> (After Effects).</li>
          <li><b>Make the sequence:</b> Premiere Pro, drag the first clip onto the <b>New Item</b> icon in the Project panel. After Effects, Composition &gt; New Composition at the same size and frame rate.</li>
          <li><b>Lay it out:</b> clips or pictures in panel order on V1, end to end. For pictures, trim each to <i>length_seconds</i> in timing.csv. If you exported separate layers, put the text on V2 and the title bar on V3.</li>
          <li><b>4K files in a 1080p sequence:</b> right-click &gt; <b>Set to Frame Size</b> (Premiere) or <kbd>Ctrl+Alt+F</kbd> / <kbd>Cmd+Opt+F</kbd> (After Effects).</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Every download also has a README.txt with these steps, written for the exact files in it.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </details>
</main>
